      "changes": 40,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/sgl-project/sglang/contents/docs%2Fcookbook%2Fautoregressive%2FXiaomi%2FMiMo-V2.6.mdx?ref=94c340235d209c54fa9bfe35ee215decba257283",
      "deletions": 1,
      "filename": "docs/cookbook/autoregressive/Xiaomi/MiMo-V2.6.mdx",
      "patch": "@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n ---\n title: MiMo-V2.6\n-description: \"Deploy MiMo-V2.6-Flash and Pro with SGLang on NVIDIA H200 and B300 GPUs, using MXFP4 MoE weights, BF16 routing, DFlash decoding, and a 1M-token context window.\"\n+description: \"Deploy MiMo-V2.6-Flash and Pro with SGLang on NVIDIA H200 and B300 or AMD MI355X GPUs, using MXFP4 MoE weights, BF16 routing, DFlash decoding, and a 1M-token context window.\"\n tag: NEW\n ---\n \n@@ -49,6 +49,44 @@ import { config } from \"/src/snippets/configs/XiaomiMiMo/mimo-v2.6.jsx\";\n \n <Deployment config={config} />\n \n+### AMD MI355X\n+\n+For MiMo-V2.6-Pro on eight MI355X GPUs, use TP8/EP8 with AITER and explicitly\n+select INT4 QuickReduce. SGLang does not enable quantized QuickReduce globally,\n+so omitting `ROCM_QUICK_REDUCE_QUANTIZATION=INT4` leaves this recipe on its\n+unquantized collective path.\n+\n+```bash Command\n+SGLANG_USE_AITER=1 \\\n+SGLANG_USE_AITER_UNIFIED_ATTN=1 \\\n+ROCM_QUICK_REDUCE_QUANTIZATION=INT4 \\\n+python -m sglang.launch_server \\\n+  --model-path XiaomiMiMo/MiMo-V2.6-Pro-RL \\\n+  --served-model-name mimo-v2.6-pro \\\n+  --tp 8 \\\n+  --ep 8 \\\n+  --moe-runner-backend aiter \\\n+  --moe-dense-tp-size 1 \\\n+  --enable-dp-lm-head \\\n+  --attention-backend aiter \\\n+  --mm-attention-backend triton_attn \\\n+  --page-size 1 \\\n+  --cuda-graph-max-bs-decode 256 \\\n+  --max-running-requests 256 \\\n+  --mem-fraction-static 0.7 \\\n+  --swa-full-tokens-ratio 0.08 \\\n+  --disable-hybrid-swa-memory \\\n+  --chunked-prefill-size 32768 \\\n+  --max-prefill-tokens 65536 \\\n+  --speculative-algorithm DFLASH \\\n+  --speculative-draft-model-path /path/to/MiMo-V2.6-Pro-RL/dflash \\\n+  --speculative-num-draft-tokens 8 \\\n+  --speculative-draft-attention-backend triton \\\n+  --reasoning-parser mimo \\\n+  --tool-call-parser mimo \\\n+  --trust-remote-code\n+```\n+\n ## Playground\n \n Experiment with reasoning and tool-call parsers, or disable speculative decoding for comparison. These overrides inherit the selected Flash or Pro recipe; they require separate validation. Parallelism and attention backends remain at the PR settings.",
